notesForOtherModules:
M9 (audit log viewer): M2 writes app events with log_audit_event as the acting user, entity 'profiles' and entity_id = the account's user id:
  - invite (new invitation, or 'Added … (existing account, no link needed)');
  - sign_in_link;
  - invite_revoke;
  - mfa_reset.
company_id is set for company-scoped events (company invitations; everything done by an owner). The summary is human-readable, e.g. 'Invited Ana Tan (ana@scaleup.my) as Fund Admin (link valid until 7 Oct 2026, 14:05)'. p_data may include link_id, purpose, expires_at, scaleup_role/company_role, link_issued and issued_by, never a token or hash. Script-issued links are logged as system events (no actor).
